# smashbin

One Rust package named `smashbin` at the repo root.

- `make` calls `~/.cargo/bin/cargo`. The Intel binary stays stamped macOS 10.12. `make` does not install. `make build-silicon` and `make build-windows` do not install. Windows uses `x86_64-pc-windows-gnu` and the MinGW linker.
- `make deb` builds glibc 2.27 Linux binaries for amd64 and arm64 and a `.deb` for each. Docker is not used. Do not install those binaries over the Mac one.
- The Homebrew formula is only in `/Users/developers/Projects/pesty-sh/homebrew-tap/Formula/smashbin.rb`. The apt repository is only in `/Users/developers/Projects/pesty-sh/apt`.
- Version 0.1.3 sets width and height. One missing side keeps the aspect ratio. It does not change output format or pad to a square. `--quality` and `--bytes` cannot be combined. They re-encode JPEG only, after the resize. A `smasher.json` or `smasher.yaml` next to the image runs each job top to bottom. `-c` selects another smasher file. Do not add a JSON, YAML, C, or `-sys` crate. PNG shrinking uses the pure-Rust `png` crate.
- No telemetry, HTTP client, update checker, or image-content logging.

Before build, install, or packaging work, read `.cursor/skills/smashbin/SKILL.md`.
